    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG are delighted to present to the market this exceptionally bright and stylish two bedroom, two bathroom apartment in The Lighthouse, a highly regarded gated development in the heart of East Wall, Dublin 3 and within touching distance of the City Centre. \n\nPresented in superb condition throughout, No. 26 has been thoughtfully modernised by its current owners and offers prospective purchasers a true turnkey opportunity. The apartment combines generous proportions with a clean, contemporary finish and an enviable South facing orientation, resulting in an abundance of natural light throughout the principal living accommodation.\n\nThe spacious living and dining area forms the heart of the property and enjoys direct access to a private South facing balcony. Large windows and glazed doors maximise the excellent aspect and frame views of the Dublin skyline and Croke Park. The kitchen is positioned just off the main living area and has been modernised to include a number of quality built in and integrated appliances. Both bedrooms are quietly positioned to the rear of the apartment and overlook the internal landscaped grounds of the development. \n\nThe main bedroom is a generous double room and benefits from its own en-suite shower room. The second bedroom is also well proportioned and is suitable as a double bedroom, guest room or home office. A separate main bathroom and an abundance of useful internal storage completes the accommodation. An additional attraction of No. 26 is its excellent B BER rating, reflecting the energy efficiency and overall quality of construction within the development. \n\nThe Lighthouse is an exceptionally well maintained and gated development with the benefit of a 24-hour security presence, attractive communal garden areas and secure underground parking with a designated space allocated for the property. \n\nThe location is particularly convenient for those working in the city centre, the IFSC, Easpoint or Docklands. The area is extremely well served by public transport, including Dublin Bus services and nearby DART and Luas connections. The Port Tunnel provides convenient access to Dublin Airport and the M1/M50 motorway network while a wide range of shops, cafés, restaurants and recreational amenities are available locally."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> READY FOR IMMEDIATE OCCUPATION</li><li> SPACIOUS 2 BED, 2 BATH APARTMENT</li><li> SOUTH FACING ASPECT</li><li> EXCEPTIONAL VIEWS</li><li> TURN KEY CONDITION THROUGHOUT</li><li> B ENERGY RATING</li><li> DESIGNATED PARKING</li><li> SECURE AND GATED DEVELOPMENT</li><li> WALKING DISTANCE TO CITY CENTRE, IFSC AND DOCKLANDS</li><li> EXCELLENT PUBLIC TRANSPORT LINKS</li><li> MGMT FEE approx 3,345 PER ANNUM TO INCLUDE SINKING FUND AND CAR PARK SERVICES</ul>"
